riscv64 zkVM: synthesized block weights for methods without profile data

Without PGO every block of a method carries the same weight (loops aside), so the inliner,
LSRA's spill costs and the callee-save decisions cannot tell an if-arm from the fall-through
path. RyuJIT's profile synthesis (AssignLikelihoods: loop back edges, throw and return
arms, 50/50 conditions) only runs under dynamic PGO or a DEBUG knob; JitZkSynthesizeCounts
(release-settable, default 0; bflat passes 1 for the zkVM libcs) runs it for every method
compiled without profile data. Measured on nine mainnet blocks: -0.45% executed steps,
identical outputs.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/fgprofile.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/fgprofile.cpp
index 46c3077ec..834d9da8e 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/fgprofile.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/fgprofile.cpp
@@ -2908,9 +2908,13 @@ PhaseStatus Compiler::fgIncorporateProfileData()
 
         // Is dynamic PGO active? If so, run synthesis.
         //
-        if (fgPgoDynamic)
+        bool synthesize = fgPgoDynamic;
+#if defined(TARGET_RISCV64)
+        synthesize |= (JitConfig.JitZkSynthesizeCounts() != 0);
+#endif
+        if (synthesize)
         {
-            JITDUMP("Dynamic PGO active, synthesizing profile data\n");
+            JITDUMP("Dynamic PGO active or synthesis requested, synthesizing profile data\n");
             ProfileSynthesis::Run(this, ProfileSynthesisOption::AssignLikelihoods);
         }
 
